From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix return-mismatch errors that gcc 14 promotes to hard errors

'return' with no value in a function returning non-void was a warning for
decades and became an error in gcc 14 (-Wreturn-mismatch), which is what the
build now trips over:

  guess-unwinder.c:95:49: error: 'return' with no value, in function returning non-void
  crash_handler.c:419:9: error: 'return' with no value, in function returning non-void

Both sites are ARM32-only code, which is why this only shows up on a 32-bit
ARM machine and never on aarch64.

Fixed rather than silenced with -Wno-error=return-mismatch, because falling off
guess_unwind_backtrace_with_ptrace() leaves an indeterminate value that the
caller consumes as a frame count:

    stack_depth = guess_unwind_backtrace_with_ptrace(...);
    if (stack_depth < 2) dump_pc_and_lr(pid, milist, stack_depth);
    dump_stack_and_code(pid, milist, stack_depth, sp_list, frame0_pc_sane);

Returning 0 matches the function's existing give-up path ("lr doesn't point to
a branch link instruction"), so a failed PTRACE_GETREGS now reports no frames
instead of garbage.

dump_pc_code() never returned a value on any path and its single caller ignores
the result, so it becomes void.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific fork of Tim Bird's crash_handler]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>

diff --git a/crash_handler.c b/crash_handler.c
index 308f0b8..98f9006 100644
--- a/crash_handler.c
+++ b/crash_handler.c
@@ -405,7 +405,7 @@ void dump_fault_addr(int pid, int sig)
     LOG("\n");
 }
 
-int dump_pc_code(int pid)
+void dump_pc_code(int pid)
 {
     struct pt_regs r;
     //pt_regs r;
diff --git a/guess-unwinder.c b/guess-unwinder.c
index cba371c..88d0024 100644
--- a/guess-unwinder.c
+++ b/guess-unwinder.c
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@ int guess_unwind_backtrace_with_ptrace(int pid, mapinfo *milist,
 	/* move up stack looking at addresses */
 
 	/* set up regs for backtrace */
-	if (ptrace(PTRACE_GETREGS, pid, 0, &r)) return;
+	if (ptrace(PTRACE_GETREGS, pid, 0, &r)) return 0;
 	sp = r.ARM_sp;
 	pc = r.ARM_pc;
 	lr = r.ARM_lr;
